{"id":"29db814da2b21ab4","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-thm-giraud.md","title":"Giraud's Theorem","display":"thm-giraud — Giraud's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-giraud","aliases":["58-thm-giraud"],"display":"thm-giraud — Giraud's Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-topos.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-zfc-cat2-equivalence-category.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-giraud"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-giraud</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-giraud — Giraud's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"78c3be29a4eab0f7\" href=\"?note=78c3be29a4eab0f7\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-topos.md\">../batch15/58-df-topos.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6477de4a04201a72\" href=\"?note=6477de4a04201a72\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-zfc-cat2-equivalence-category.md\">../batch06/58-df-zfc-cat2-equivalence-category.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal E,U,\\mathcal C,J,Q\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal E,U,\\mathcal C,J,Q\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)\">\\(\\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)\\)</span> (universe-indexed Grothendieck-topos predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)\">\\(\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J)\">\\(\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S\\)</span> (site, sheaf-category, and equivalence predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}giraud\\text{-}site}\\vdash \\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\mathcal C,J,Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)\\land\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S(Q,\\mathcal E,\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J))\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}giraud\\text{-}site}\\vdash \\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\mathcal C,J,Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)\\land\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S(Q,\\mathcal E,\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J))\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The site representation uses the exact universe, topology, and equivalence-witness parameters required upstream. The former intrinsic clause was removed because the network has no registered formal predicates for its four component Giraud conditions; retaining a prose-only <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GiraudAxioms}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{GiraudAxioms}_S\\)</span> would falsely present them as formalized.</li>\n<li>The site is not unique; the conclusion is categorical equivalence, not equality.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-topos.md","status":"resolved","id":"78c3be29a4eab0f7","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-topos.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-zfc-cat2-equivalence-category.md","status":"resolved","id":"6477de4a04201a72","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-zfc-cat2-equivalence-category.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal E,U,\\mathcal C,J,Q\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}giraud\\text{-}site}\\vdash \\operatorname{GrothendieckTopos}_S(\\mathcal E,U)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\mathcal C,J,Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Site}_S(\\mathcal C,J,U)\\land\\mathrm{ZfcCat2EquivalenceCategory}_S(Q,\\mathcal E,\\operatorname{Sh}_U(\\mathcal C,J))\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GiraudAxioms}_S","display":false}],"bytes":1363,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4182","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-thm-giraud.md|58-thm-giraud]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["78c3be29a4eab0f7","6477de4a04201a72"]}